{"text": "RIVERBEND COMMUNITY FOOD PANTRY -- DONOR NOTES, SPRING APPEAL\nkept by Paz Villaseñor, bookkeeper (part-time)      EIN 23-7741980\nfor the Form 990 / Schedule B file and year-end acknowledgment letters\n\nMay 4, 2026\n* Constance Abernathy-Wolfe -- mailed check #3318 for $5,000.00, dated 4/30/2026.\n  Same as last year. She is 97 now and her daughter handles the checkbook; the\n  thank-you goes to Mrs. Abernathy-Wolfe at Willow Glen Retirement Residence, Rm 214,\n  88 Front Street, Lewisburg, PA 17837. NO phone calls (hard of hearing).\n  Needs written acknowledgment per IRC § 170(f)(8) since it is over the threshold.\n\n* Olufemi Family Charitable Fund (donor-advised, at Keystone Heritage Securities) --\n  grant $12,500 recommended by Grace Olufemi. Grant ID KHS-DAF-0092741.\n  No tax letter to Grace personally -- the fund is the donor. She asked that\n  it be listed as anonymous in the annual report.\n\nMay 6, 2026\n* Hyun-woo Park -- phoned in a card gift, $250 monthly starting now.\n  Card 4985 5081 6529 6933  exp 08/29  code 611  billing zip 17801\n  (PAZ -- SHRED THIS PAGE after entering in the processor. We are not supposed\n  to keep the code.)  His email hwpark@susqmail.example. Employer match through\n  Allegheny Ridge Tool & Die, Inc. -- he will send their form.\n\n* Stock gift: Leonard and Miriam Feinstein, 140 shares of an index fund,\n  transferred 05/01/2026 from their account KH-4471-88203 at Keystone Heritage\n  to ours (KH-9020-11467). Mean of high/low that day x 140 = $19,362.00.\n  Letter must describe the shares and NOT state a value. They will need\n  Form 8283. The gift is in honor of their grandson's bar mitzvah at\n  Temple Beth Shalom of Riverbend; Mr. Feinstein wants the temple's\n  social action committee copied. (Leonard Feinstein, 570-555-0131.)\n\nMay 11, 2026\n* Cash, $1,840, Friday collection from Riverbend Islamic Center, dropped off by\n  the imam's assistant. Receipt no. R-2026-0417 issued to the Center, not\n  to individuals.\n* Laborers' Local 1180 -- check $750.00 from the members' relief fund,\n  delivered by Walter Dumbrowski, the local's business agent. Walt also\n  dropped off a personal $100 in cash. Receipt in his name, home address\n  R.R. 2 Box 118, Mifflinburg PA 17844.\n* Teddy Kalani -- online, $40. Came in through the Giving Tuesday page that\n  is somehow still live: https://give.riverbendpantry.example/donate?c=gt25\n  Ask the web volunteer to take it down. Processor shows donor IP 192.0.2.146\n  and flagged it as possible card testing; it was a real gift, he called.\n\nMay 13, 2026 -- PROBLEMS / QUESTIONS FOR THE TREASURER\n1. Mrs. Feinstein asked whether we could \"pass along\" $500 of their\n   gift to the Susquehanna Valley Democratic Committee dinner. NO. We are a\n   501(c)(3); we cannot touch that. I told her politely. Please back me up.\n2. Mr. Park wrote on his pledge card that he is giving \"in thanks,\n   5 years sober this month.\" Lovely, but it should not go in the newsletter. I\n   blacked it out on the scanned copy.\n3. A walk-in donor who would only give her first name (Dolores) left a\n   cashier's check for ten thousand dollars even. No address. Pub. 1771\n   says we cannot force it; I logged it as anonymous. Bank deposit slip\n   shows our account 0044-718-2260 at the credit union, deposited 5/12/26.\n4. Board member asked for \"the list of who gave what.\" Schedule B names are\n   not public. I will give totals only: $40,142.00 for the appeal so far.\n\nPaz -- pantry.books@riverbendpantry.example -- Tues/Thurs only -- 570 555 0109", "kind": "Text file", "detail": "565 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Paz Villaseñor", "Constance Abernathy-Wolfe", "Grace Olufemi", "Hyun-woo Park", "Leonard Feinstein", "Miriam Feinstein", "Walter Dumbrowski", "Dolores"], "companies": ["RIVERBEND COMMUNITY FOOD PANTRY", "Keystone Heritage Securities", "Allegheny Ridge Tool & Die, Inc.", "Temple Beth Shalom of Riverbend", "Riverbend Islamic Center", "Riverbend Pantry", "Susquehanna Valley Democratic Committee", "Credit Union"]}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "importMs": 0.09999999962747097, "modelMs": 35745.199999999255, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "passport_dl", "routing", "phone", "record", "vin", "account", "money", "dob", "age90", "date", "street", "zip", "postal_ca", "names"], "detections": [{"start": 0, "end": 31, "text": "RIVERBEND COMMUNITY FOOD PANTRY", "kind": "company", "source": "model", "canonical": "RIVERBEND COMMUNITY FOOD PANTRY"}, {"start": 70, "end": 84, "text": "Paz Villaseñor", "kind": "person", "source": "model", "canonical": "Paz Villaseñor"}, {"start": 118, "end": 128, "text": "23-7741980", "kind": "ein", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "23-7741980"}, {"start": 201, "end": 212, "text": "May 4, 2026", "kind": "date", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "May 4, 2026"}, {"start": 215, "end": 240, "text": "Constance Abernathy-Wolfe", "kind": "person", "source": "model", "canonical": "Constance Abernathy-Wolfe"}, {"start": 267, "end": 276, "text": "$5,000.00", "kind": "money", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "$5,000.00"}, {"start": 284, "end": 293, "text": "4/30/2026", "kind": "date", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "4/30/2026"}, {"start": 399, "end": 414, "text": "Abernathy-Wolfe", "kind": "person", "source": "short-form", "canonical": "Constance Abernathy-Wolfe"}, {"start": 462, "end": 477, "text": "88 Front Street", "kind": "street", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "88 Front Street"}, {"start": 493, "end": 498, "text": "17837", "kind": "zip", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "17837"}, {"start": 620, "end": 627, "text": "Olufemi", "kind": "person", "source": "short-form", "canonical": "Grace Olufemi"}, {"start": 670, "end": 698, "text": "Keystone Heritage Securities", "kind": "company", "source": "model", "canonical": "Keystone Heritage Securities"}, {"start": 711, "end": 718, "text": "$12,500", "kind": "money", "s